.TH DANBY-PRODUCTIONEXCHANGE 1
.SH NAME
danby-productionexchange \- production, use, and exchange of two goods
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/productionexchange
.SH MODEL
X'=pX-cX X-k(X-Y);
Y'=pY-cY Y+k(X-Y).
.PP
X and Y are inventories produced and consumed in two sectors.  Exchange moves
goods from the larger inventory toward the smaller without creating or
destroying their combined stock.  Thus (X+Y)'=pX+pY-cX X-cY Y independently
of the exchange coefficient k.
.SH DISPLAY
Both inventories and their current values are shown.  Increasing exchange
equalizes shortages and surpluses more rapidly but does not change total
production or use.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag either inventory bar.  Tracks set both production and use rates and the
exchange response.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
Cancellation of internal exchange in the total-stock balance is tested by
.B temple/danbytest.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/productionexchange.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/productionexchange.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR populationmodel (2),
.IR numerics (2)
